00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.190
Would you rather stay
in a hotel or a motel

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.640
and what's the difference?

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.470
- Great question. Motel all the way.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.370
- Why?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.250
- First of all, I drive everywhere.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.010
I drove here. It took
me 20 hours to get here.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.680
I'm a driver. I like to
park the car in front.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.640
- You know, in Los Angeles,

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.210
it takes you 20 hours to
get anywhere, you know?

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.710
- Yeah, I live there and yes it does,

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:37.543
you're correct.

00:02:37.543 --> 00:02:38.670
- As you are traveling around,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.530
as you're looking at
different hotels and motels,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.810
what's a trend that needs to go?

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.620
- Oh, this is a great question.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.420
I hate a popcorn ceiling.
I think everyone does.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.310
- Mm hmm.
- Oh the carpet.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.370
Listen, the carpet that
has the design in it,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.400
so you can't see that your
kids puked everywhere.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.233
- Yeah.
- Ew.

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:54.520
- Yeah. That's terrible.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.520
Do carpet, tile, or hardwood.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.000
- Do you watch yourself?

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.840
- I'd like to be cool and say no,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.520
but yes I absolutely.
- Yes you absolutely do.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.363
Who wouldn't?

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.370
What's the number one tip
for people who are looking at

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.460
that wall or that project
and thinking, "Ugh."

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.280
- Paint! Gotta use paint.
- Really?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.900
- Paint's cheap. It's easy.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.870
You can fix it relatively, like,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.898
it's not a ton of commitment,

00:03:17.898 --> 00:03:19.920
and you can grab a paintbrush,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.810
you can just start
splotching on some stuff

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.820
and make some wallpaper looking.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.653
I do that in the workshop.

00:03:24.653 --> 00:03:25.580
- Really?
- Yeah!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.670
- What's the color right now
that you would recommend?

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.220
Like the hot color of the moment?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.480
- I mean, dark colors.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.410
Like a dark maroon, a dark
plum, something like that.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.050
- What's different about Texas design?

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:36.580
I mean we're here in Waco.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.890
Do you bring in sort of Texas

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.260
into your DIY and your home decor?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.560
- I've done a little shiplap in my houses,

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.140
but I like doing it vertical,

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.610
to do a little bit different
than the Texas style, but.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.120
- Can you spell Texas backwards?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.010
- Oh, this is my nightmare

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.820
from middle school spelling bee.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.740
S, A, S, E.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.410
S-A-X.
(laughing)

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.829
E-T.
(bell dinging)

00:04:01.829 --> 00:04:02.662
- You got it, you got it.

00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:04.330
You got it! Thanks so much.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.340
Everyone watch "Handcrafted
Home Projects,"

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.440
Jenni Yolo, on Magnolia.
(upbeat music)

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.400
Let me ask you a question about flowers.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.130
Carnations, tacky or underrated?

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.010
- Love them. Love them.
- See? See?

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.740
- They last forever.
- Mm hmm.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.570
- Come in all sorts of colors.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.830
They get a bad rep, but
they're one of my faves.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.250
- So many times I get flowers

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.470
and then I feel like a day
later they're already wilted.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:29.620
So what can we do to keep
our flowers to last longer?

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.190
- Well, you know what,
you gotta think about it.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.720
Like, would you wanna be
sat in stagnant water?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.510
Change that water every day.
- Mm hmm.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.900
- Give them a little
snip, maybe change them.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.110
If they're in direct light,
take them out of direct light.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.790
- All right, and what do
you do to keep it fresh

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.740
on "Art In Bloom"?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.050
- That's a good question.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.710
I try and challenge myself.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.930
So we've changed it up.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.260
We're trying to do something
different for each episode.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.760
Give people new skill sets to take away.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.810
Yeah, not to put too much
pressure on yourself.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.380
- See, I think people
bring so much pressure

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.720
when they're trying to
make things beautiful,

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.100
but it can be easy, it can
be fun, and it can be doable.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.120
And you're showing us how to do it.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.470
Thank you so much.
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:04.733
My absolute pleasure.
(upbeat music)

